{"title":"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that the complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b1ac9f729910eeb585972547f596db1efe0224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|z\\right| = \\left|z^2+1\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"101\" height=\"22\" />.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37d345c5c4dc4bd651c7f87a5e7396ec9ec2d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|z\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"21\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbf54eac904c649c577ad3fb7c9cbaa0c0090fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K^4$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec32b83c7b36e6db008f7c885a292dcf5235c663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{r+\\sqrt{s}}{t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4d8cb6aa374535cea16c712b70c8f6ba8155ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s+t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d824506d08bdcc9b7897ef78aff7a689d06ae54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdea1d77a02ff5dff1f619df844e7a907c3635d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = \\frac{\\left|z^2+1\\right|}{\\left|z\\right|} = \\left|\\frac{z^2+1}{z}\\right| = \\left|z+\\frac{1}{z}\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"262\" height=\"43\" />.  Now, consider that we may write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d42a98687db6ba771b8d7d697b34cf7b40cac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = re^{i\\theta}=r\\left(\\cos(\\theta)+i\\sin(\\theta)\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> a positive real number so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589ce64262af3e406738a2e8b8731028678adb68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z| = r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> some real number.  Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde51042fb4ab8da65dd37d532c199ccce283356.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|z+\\frac{1}{z}\\right| = \\left|re^{i\\theta} + \\frac{1}{r}\\cdot e^{-i\\theta}\\right|= \\left|r\\left(\\cos(\\theta)+i\\sin(\\theta)\\right)+\\frac{1}{r}\\left(\\cos(-\\theta)+i\\sin(-\\theta)\\right)\\right|\\]\" width=\"588\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af96a7336db4253afe203f9ea1ad24abcdcbe9e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\left|r\\left(\\cos(\\theta)+i\\sin(\\theta)\\right)+\\frac{1}{r}\\left(\\cos(\\theta)-i\\sin(\\theta)\\right)\\right|=\\left|\\left(r+\\frac{1}{r}\\right) \\cos(\\theta) +\\left(r-\\frac{1}{r}\\right)i\\sin(\\theta)\\right|\\]\" width=\"662\" height=\"43\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bc09d2aef1115f363934106f3af83fa280981f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=  \\sqrt{\\left(r+\\frac{1}{r}\\right)^2\\cos^2(\\theta)+\\left(r-\\frac{1}{r}\\right)^2\\sin^2(\\theta)}=\\sqrt{\\left(r^2+\\frac{1}{r^2}\\right)\\left(\\cos^2(\\theta)+\\sin^2(\\theta)\\right)+2\\left(\\cos^2(\\theta)-\\sin^2(\\theta)\\right)}\\]\" width=\"784\" height=\"55\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fee3153a57a682dcde4b9d9bd563ef899bb7a6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sqrt{r^2+\\frac{1}{r^2} + 2\\cos(2\\theta)}.\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"43\" />  Since we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497db753e30e52a384cab6b18f73655ca731342f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|z+\\frac{1}{z}\\right| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"89\" height=\"43\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b363a6a9a87e8f0feee7092ea23d2b721a0a816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2+\\frac{1}{r^2} + 2\\cos(2\\theta) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"181\" height=\"37\" />, or equivalently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8331cef0ec67ab42d39a9f40bebb0df4849b8e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^4 + \\left(2\\cos(2\\theta) - 1\\right)r^2 + 1 =0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"19\" />.  By the quadratic equation, this has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20ff7d08dcf374268eeff9240377fdf4a078e11f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 = \\frac{1-2\\cos(2\\theta)\\pm \\sqrt{ \\left(2\\cos(2\\theta) - 1\\right)^2-4}}{2},\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"52\" /> and to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we take the larger root <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a796361ff725caa96122e7d1be2c66776da679f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 = \\frac{1-2\\cos(2\\theta)+\\sqrt{ \\left(2\\cos(2\\theta) - 1\\right)^2-4}}{2}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"51\" /> which is clearly maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52a2d2182832570b95b99d51ec9b3e7e4ed95142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos(2\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is minimized.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24be6588299881ab732472b0c69b836a7dd8e79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1\\le \\cos(2\\theta)\\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> will occur where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f8aab1cdca8ea8b209ded5b350628c1570d3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cos(2\\theta) = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, so the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> occurs where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/07424f071ea1eb682afa5dbed0d5f8b1b082dd87.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"41\" /> and finally we find that the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e5b98d00879f9ad03a91126f7c89acff7c32ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|=r&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9018975043fdb723cf817ddbaeef9e1331a541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r= \\sqrt{\\frac{3+\\sqrt{5}}{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6+2\\sqrt{5}}}{2} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{2},\\text{  the golden ratio.}\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"53\" /> Taking the fourth power, the desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb3148488885ac5a648c89d99b94c679ea18110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{7+\\sqrt{45}}{2} \\implies r+s+t=\\boxed{054}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"249\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f67554c5555fa4d14b57df4ddc6de92902a3d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=re^{i\\theta}$\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/113f9bcdca5b349b43ec22894e7d468b4b2f8cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|^2 = r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>To compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6bebee050d29599763b8b1f31adbc98ab11043ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^2+1|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"19\" />, connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3b0b966fdafe902c6375ebef2b7fa9fdc4d223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> to the origin and construct an altitude to the x-axis. Extend this line one unit above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3b0b966fdafe902c6375ebef2b7fa9fdc4d223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and connect that point to the origin to create <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fdcbae166da009fa0b34e377a4b33f471488a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we use the Law of Cosines on the triangle with vertices at the origin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3b0b966fdafe902c6375ebef2b7fa9fdc4d223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fdcbae166da009fa0b34e377a4b33f471488a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" />, giving\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c0889e7fe11460b9c6b099462f791484363951d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z^2+1|^2 = r^4 + 1 - 2r^2 \\cos(2\\theta+90) = r^4 + 2r^2 \\sin(2\\theta)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"460\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>(or you could use the Pythagorean Theorem). Either way, we proceed from here as we did with Solution 1 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/b/d0bae13d8813291bb4530788742882619eb56700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s + t = \\boxed{054}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-Solution by <b>thecmd999</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 9\"> Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems/Problem 7\"> Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_I_2012_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME I 2012 Problems\">Mock AIME I 2012 Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017113928\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 221/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8459/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10997:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017113928 and revision id 244737. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}